quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  39,75,"And you will see the angels encircling around the Throne, glorifying the praise of their Lord. Then, the judgement will be passed between them with justice. And it will be said: ‘All praise belongs to Allah, the Lord of all worlds.’"
  40,1,Ha-Mim.
  40,2,"The revelation of this Book is from Allah, the All-Mighty, the All-Knowing,"
  40,3,"Forgiver of sins, Acceptor of repentance, Severe in retribution, Lord of bounty. There is no god except Him; (and) towards Him is the eventual destination."
  40,4,No one disputes the Signs of Allah except the disbelievers. So let it not astonish you that they move back and forth in the towns.
  40,5,"The people of Nuh (Noah) denied (the truth) before them, and (so did) the (heathen) factions after them. And every community intended to seize and destroy its messenger. And they disputed through falsehood to refute the truth. Then, I seized and destroyed them. So how was My retribution?"
  40,6,"That is how your Lord’s Word proved true against the disbelievers, that they would be the inhabitants of the Fire."
  40,7,"Those who carry the Throne and those around it glorify the praise of their Lord. They believe in Him and seek forgiveness for the believers (praying): ‘Our Lord! You encompass all things in mercy and knowledge. So forgive those who repent and follow Your path, and save them from the punishment of the Hellfire."
